NAME
    nano - simple full-screen text editor

SYNOPSIS
    nano <path>

DESCRIPTION
    A small full-screen editor for creating/editing a real file (a 'source'
    script, say) without leaving the shell for an external editor. NOT a
    full GNU nano clone - no search, no cut/paste ring, no syntax
    highlighting - just arrow-key movement, insert/Backspace/Delete, and
    Ctrl+O to save / Ctrl+X to exit (prompting to save first if there are
    unsaved changes). <path> is created if it doesn't exist yet, and is
    walled to the project's own directory tree like every other real-file
    command here (see 'cd'). Needs a REAL interactive terminal - it takes
    over the console with raw key reads and full-screen redraws the same
    way this shell's own line editor does for a single line, just for a
    whole buffer - so it refuses cleanly (rather than failing strangely) when
    stdin/stdout is redirected (a piped script, a 'source'd file, a headless
    test) or when there's no real terminal at all (EmuSen.Mistress's GUI
    console window).

EXAMPLES
    nano setup.txt
